    "chr21 reading": "`genomeos.genome.annotation.default_gencode` prefers the distilled chr21+chrM subset whenever the chromosomes asked for are within {chr21, chrM}, and that file lives at data/results/gencode_v50_chr21_chrM.gff3.gz. The census builds its declared groups from the traced reads BY PATH PREFIX, and `data/results/` is the first group's prefix, so chr21's annotation was declared in group 1 (`the all-enhancer sweep's committed per-chromosome results`, 70 members = 3 x 23 sweep files + this one) instead of group 3 (`GENCODE 50 per-chromosome annotation`, 22 members). The comparator for chr21 WAS read and IS declared; the group LABEL is wrong about it. 22 = 24 - chrY (never opened) - chr21 (declared under the other group's label)."
  },
